{"verdict": "revise",
  "hypothesis_status": {"H1": "refuted", "H2": "supported", "H3": "refuted"},
  "issues": ["C1/E1 misreads the data: the rows show Oct 22 02:00 UTC (21:00 CDT) USGS peak 5,640 cfs, NWM NULL, NWS Oliver 1,232.5 cfs. The finding claims 'NWM peaked one hour later at 5,516 cfs' but E1 rows show NWM is NULL through 06:00 UTC Oct 23. NWM has no data for Oct 22 CDT per ground-truth facts. C2/E2 correctly confirms USGS and NWS Oliver share the same tailwater stage sensor (stage_diff_ft ≤ 0.04 ft), but the finding's claim that 'derived flows differ substantially' with NWS 300–400 cfs higher is contradicted by E2 rows on Oct 18 where NWS 1,202.5 cfs vs USGS 676.0 cfs at 07:00 UTC (22:00 CDT) — the discrepancy direction and magnitude vary by hour, not systematic. C3/E3 misidentifies the peak hour: the rows show Oct 18 has peaks at hours 3, 6, 9, 10, 17, 20, 21, 22, 23 CDT — 21:00 CDT is one of many hours, not a consistent recurrence. Ground-truth facts confirm Oct 18 peak at 21:00 CDT (8,180 cfs) but the finding overgeneralizes from a single day. C4/E4 correctly quantifies the daily mean gap (279–448 cfs NWS higher) and negligible stage change, supporting H2. C5/E5 misreads peak hours: rows show Oct 18 peaks at hours 3, 6, 9, 10, 17, 23 CDT with 21:00 (hour 21) listed as 8 cfs, not 8,180 cfs. The finding claims 'no consistent 21:00 CDT recurrence' but ground-truth facts state Oct 18 peak at 21:00 CDT. C6/E6 correctly shows +1 h lag and magnitude match on Oct 23–24, but the finding's claim that 'NWM reverted to near-baseflow' contradicts ground-truth: Oct 23 USGS peak 5,640 cfs at 19:00 CDT, NWM 5,399 cfs at 20:00 CDT (1 h later), not near-baseflow.", "new_checks": [{"id": "C7", "hypothesis": "H1", "purpose": "Confirm NWM has no data for Oct 22 CDT by checking hr_utc range where NWM is NULL vs where USGS shows the 5,640 cfs pulse at 21:00 CDT.", "how": "SELECT COUNT(*) as null_hours, COUNT(nwm_cfs) as has_data FROM water.hourly_compare WHERE hr_utc BETWEEN '2026-10-23 02:00' AND '2026-10-23 06:00' AND nwm_cfs IS NULL"}, {"id": "C8", "hypothesis": "H3", "purpose": "Extract the exact CDT hour of the daily maximum 15-min peak for each day Oct 18–24 and test if 21:00 CDT occurs more frequently than chance (expected 1/24 ≈ 4%).", "how": "SELECT date_format(from_utc_timestamp(to_timestamp(hr_utc, 'yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm'), 'America/Chicago'), 'HH') as peak_hr_cdt, COUNT(*) as day_count FROM (SELECT hr_utc, MAX(usgs_northport_peak_cfs) over (PARTITION BY date_format(from_utc_timestamp(to_timestamp(hr_utc, 'yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm'), 'America/Chicago'), 'yyyy-MM-dd')) as daily_peak FROM water.hourly_compare WHERE hr_utc BETWEEN '2026-10-18 06:00' AND '2026-10-25 06:00' AND usgs_northport_peak_cfs IS NOT NULL GROUP BY hr_utc) GROUP BY peak_hr_cdt ORDER BY day_count DESC LIMIT 24"}]}
